# Prompt
Regenerate the VERIFICATION CRITERIA for this brownfield story. Your previous verification criteria were FLAGGED and must be fixed:
- VC 1 references internal function getGreeting() — restate as what the greeting displays, not how it is produced

THE FIX SITE (located by the code-graph detective — anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces):
- src/hello.ts :: getGreeting — getGreeting COMPUTES the greeting value — it returns the hard-coded literal 'hello world', which is the exact wrong value the ticket reports (should be 'hello dolly'). It is not a display or mapper layer; the incorrect string originates in this function body, and its only caller plus the test in src/hello.test.ts merely consume whatever it returns.
Do NOT write criteria about areas unrelated to this code.


Acceptance criteria (IMMUTABLE — the intent to verify; do NOT restate as-is, VERIFY them):
